import{_ as e,o as a,c as r,a0 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BTg7EidG.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Skills & Research","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guide/skills.md","filePath":"guide/skills.md"}'),h={name:"guide/skills.md"};function o(d,t,n,i,l,c){return a(),r("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[s('<h1 id="skills-research" tabindex="-1">Skills &amp; Research <a class="header-anchor" href="#skills-research" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Skills &amp; Research&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="where-each-art-is-taught" tabindex="-1">Where each art is taught <a class="header-anchor" href="#where-each-art-is-taught" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Where each art is taught&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Town Hall</strong> teaches one art per class per tier — the old three. Everything else is taught where the trade actually lives, which is a reason to raise those structures beyond drilling in them:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Building</th><th>What it teaches</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Barracks</strong></td><td>Blinding Dust, Bulwark, Lookout, The Long Column</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Laboratory</strong></td><td>Quickening Balm, Vitriol Flask, Quicken, Mend the Column, Immovable Object, Unstoppable Force</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Shadow Guild</strong></td><td>Shadow Step, Assassinate, Poison Blade, Steal</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Bestiary</strong></td><td>Beast Bond, Wild Heart, Ensnare</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Nothing is innate</p><p>Your Lord begins with steel and a title, not a technique. <strong>Every</strong> skill is studied at a Town Hall — including your own class&#39;s art, which is simply the cheapest project on the list and the one to start with.</p></div><p>Every hero carries up to <strong>three skills</strong>, and every one of them is studied first and assigned afterward from the unit sheet — including the art of their own class.</p><h2 id="where-an-art-is-worked" tabindex="-1">Where an art is worked <a class="header-anchor" href="#where-an-art-is-worked" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Where an art is worked&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Every art belongs to one of three arenas, and the <strong>Skills</strong> button on the command dock gathers all three in one sheet:</p><ul><li><strong>Always</strong> — passives, simply true while the hero lives. Rally, Shield Wall, Plunder, Field Mending.</li><li><strong>In battle</strong> — thrown on the field, spending that hero&#39;s action. They appear as chips in the battle dock on their turn.</li><li><strong>On the map</strong> — worked between fights, from the Skills sheet. One a day per hero.</li></ul><h2 id="essence-what-an-art-costs" tabindex="-1">Essence: what an art costs <a class="header-anchor" href="#essence-what-an-art-costs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Essence: what an art costs&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Every soldier carries Essence</strong>, not only the alchemists — a warrior starts with 12, a rogue 14, a keeper 16, an adept 20, and it grows with every level. It is what arts are paid from, and it is the only thing stopping a hero throwing a net every single turn.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Art</th><th>Costs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Shadow Step, Lookout, Steal</td><td>3 ✨</td></tr><tr><td>Ensnare, Blinding Dust, Quicken</td><td>4 ✨</td></tr><tr><td>Quickening Balm</td><td>5 ✨</td></tr><tr><td>Vitriol Flask, Assassinate, Immovable Object</td><td>6 ✨</td></tr><tr><td>Unstoppable Force</td><td>8 ✨</td></tr><tr><td>Mend the Column</td><td>10 ✨</td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>Transmute Blast</em> is the exception: it spends <strong>half your whole pool</strong> and deals that as damage, so its price is its effect.</p><h2 id="craft-what-an-art-is-worth" tabindex="-1">Craft: what an art is worth <a class="header-anchor" href="#craft-what-an-art-is-worth" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Craft: what an art is worth&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Essence is what an art <em>costs</em>. <strong>Craft (⚗)</strong> is what it is <em>worth</em>. The two damages are separate: steel and bowstring on one side, the working on the other. A Transmute Blast lands for half your pool <strong>plus your craft</strong>; a vitriol flask and a quickening balm both add it too.</p><p>Adepts carry the most craft and gain more with every level; keepers carry some; a rogue a little; a warrior none. A <strong>staff</strong> is the way to buy more of it, and it charges you melee and reach for the privilege — see <a href="/athanor-docs/guide/artifacts.html">Arms &amp; Artifacts</a>.</p><p><strong>Essence comes back a fifth as fast as blood, and only where blood does</strong> — standing on your own territory, or under <em>Field Mending</em>. Recovering your arts means going home. Plan a campaign around it: a hero who spends everything in one fight is carrying dead weight for the next several days.</p><div class="tip custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">The Philosopher&#39;s Stone</p><p>Its bearer&#39;s Essence never runs down — but the working comes out of <strong>them</strong> instead, a third of the price in blood. It can never be the blow that kills them. See <a href="/athanor-docs/guide/artifacts.html">Arms &amp; Artifacts</a>.</p></div><h2 id="how-research-works" tabindex="-1">How research works <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-research-works" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How research works&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Research happens at the <strong>Town Hall</strong> of any city you own; the hall&#39;s level is the city&#39;s level, and it gates what can be studied:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Hall level</th><th>Opens</th><th>Cost</th><th>Time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>The class arts (tier 1)</td><td>60🪙 4💎</td><td>2 days</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>The deeper studies (tier 2)</td><td>150🪙 10💎</td><td>5 days</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>The masterworks (tier 3)</td><td>200🪙 16💎</td><td>6 days</td></tr></tbody></table><p>One project sits on the bench at a time, guild-wide. Once a skill is mastered it belongs to the whole guild forever: <strong>any hero of the right class</strong> can assign it from their unit sheet, from that day on, and a mastered skill can be unassigned and reassigned freely.</p><h2 id="the-warrior-s-line" tabindex="-1">The warrior&#39;s line <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-warrior-s-line" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The warrior&#39;s line&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Tier</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>📣 Rally</td><td>1</td><td>The whole party fights at +2 attack and +2 defense while this hero leads</td></tr><tr><td>🛡 Shield Wall</td><td>2</td><td>The party braces at +3 defense whenever it is the one attacked</td></tr><tr><td>📯 Warcry</td><td>3</td><td>The enemy line falters: every foe fights at −2 defense</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Warriors anchor a line. Rally is always on; Shield Wall turns a garrisoned warrior hero into a wall worth breaking armies on; Warcry is the siege-breaker, softening a deep garrison before the blades cross. Rally and Warcry together swing every exchange by four points.</p><h2 id="the-rogue-s-line" tabindex="-1">The rogue&#39;s line <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-rogue-s-line" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The rogue&#39;s line&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Tier</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>🌫 Ambush</td><td>1</td><td>A free opening volley whenever this party attacks, +15% to a fleeing Lord&#39;s escape, and ambushes are sprung more often</td></tr><tr><td>🪙 Plunder</td><td>2</td><td>Hoards turn up in 60% of taken holds instead of 40%, and dungeon chests run half again as rich</td></tr><tr><td>⚔ Overwhelm</td><td>3</td><td>The class counter (warrior beats rogue beats alchemist beats warrior) deals double damage instead of half again, for the whole party</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Rogues profit from initiative and greed. Ambush makes every attack begin a step ahead; Plunder pays for itself within a few raids, and it belongs on whichever hero storms the most holds; Overwhelm rewards building a party that counters what your enemy fields. Rogue heroes also sneak parties past dungeon floors, and flee down stairs mid-fight.</p><h2 id="the-alchemist-s-line" tabindex="-1">The alchemist&#39;s line <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-alchemist-s-line" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The alchemist&#39;s line&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Tier</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>⚗️ Transmute Blast</td><td>1</td><td>Opens battle by burning half the hero&#39;s Essence as damage that ignores armor (on the tactical field, a cast at range 3)</td></tr><tr><td>🩹 Field Mending</td><td>2</td><td>The whole party heals an extra 10% of max HP every day, even on the march</td></tr><tr><td>🌀 Quicksilver March</td><td>3</td><td>The hero&#39;s craft lightens every boot: the party marches +3 move points a day</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Alchemists win wars between the battles. Transmute Blast scales with Essence, so a leveled alchemist Lord opens with a thunderclap; Field Mending keeps a campaigning army whole without ever going home; and Quicksilver March makes one army fight like two by arriving first. Put March on the party that answers threats, and Mending on the one that never stops pushing.</p><h2 id="the-arts-taught-in-the-trade-halls" tabindex="-1">The arts taught in the trade halls <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-arts-taught-in-the-trade-halls" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The arts taught in the trade halls&quot;">​</a></h2><p>These are not on the Town Hall&#39;s bench. Each is studied where its trade lives, which is the reason to raise those buildings past drilling in them. Most are <strong>active</strong> — used on the battlefield, spending the hero&#39;s turn.</p><h3 id="barracks-·-the-warrior-s-yard" tabindex="-1">Barracks · the warrior&#39;s yard <a class="header-anchor" href="#barracks-·-the-warrior-s-yard" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Barracks · the warrior&#39;s yard&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Tier</th><th>Used?</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>💨 Blinding Dust</td><td>2</td><td>active</td><td>Grit in a foe&#39;s eyes: their blows go wide half the time for two turns</td></tr><tr><td>🧱 Bulwark</td><td>3</td><td>passive</td><td>A hero who spends their turn holding ground gives +2 guard to every ally beside them</td></tr><tr><td>🚩 The Long Column</td><td>3</td><td>passive</td><td>This hero leads <strong>ten</strong> soldiers instead of eight</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>The Long Column</strong> is the one art that changes the shape of an army rather than the outcome of a swing, and it belongs to whoever is actually leading: a second hero marching in the ranks carrying it adds nothing. Split them off into a banner of their own and the two extra places go with them.</p><h3 id="laboratory-·-the-alchemist-s-bench" tabindex="-1">Laboratory · the alchemist&#39;s bench <a class="header-anchor" href="#laboratory-·-the-alchemist-s-bench" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Laboratory · the alchemist&#39;s bench&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Tier</th><th>Used?</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>💧 Quickening Balm</td><td>2</td><td>active</td><td>Lays a balm over a patch of ground that settles a few battlefield turns later and heals every ally standing in it</td></tr><tr><td>⏱ Quicken</td><td>2</td><td>active</td><td>Hurries one ally: they come round in the turn order much sooner</td></tr><tr><td>🧪 Vitriol Flask</td><td>3</td><td>active</td><td>Hurls a flask that eats everything in a three-tile square — friend and foe alike, so mind the throw</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Quickening Balm is shared: learning it opens it for <strong>Beastmasters</strong> too, though in their hands it tends only the beasts.</p><h3 id="shadow-guild-·-the-rogue-s-trade" tabindex="-1">Shadow Guild · the rogue&#39;s trade <a class="header-anchor" href="#shadow-guild-·-the-rogue-s-trade" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Shadow Guild · the rogue&#39;s trade&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Tier</th><th>Used?</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>🌑 Shadow Step</td><td>2</td><td>active</td><td>Melts into cover: much harder to hit until this hero&#39;s next turn</td></tr><tr><td>🗡 Assassinate</td><td>3</td><td>active</td><td>A killing blow struck from behind a foe — or from above. Nothing from the front</td></tr><tr><td>🧪 Poison Blade</td><td>3</td><td>passive</td><td>This hero&#39;s blows leave a wound that keeps bleeding for three battlefield turns</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="bestiary-·-the-keeper-s-arts" tabindex="-1">Bestiary · the keeper&#39;s arts <a class="header-anchor" href="#bestiary-·-the-keeper-s-arts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Bestiary · the keeper&#39;s arts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The <strong>Beastmaster</strong> is a calling of its own — hired at a Bestiary, never mustered, and no guild is led by one. Beast Bond and Wild Heart are theirs alone, and only once they are raised to hero.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Tier</th><th>Used?</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>🕸 Ensnare</td><td>2</td><td>active</td><td>Throws a net over one foe: they cannot take a step for two turns, though they can still fight</td></tr><tr><td>🐾 Beast Bond</td><td>2</td><td>passive</td><td>Every beast in this hero&#39;s party fights at +3 attack and +3 defense</td></tr><tr><td>🫀 Wild Heart</td><td>3</td><td>passive</td><td>Beasts in this party keep for half the gold, and mend 15% of their health each day</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Trades overlap.</strong> <em>Ensnare</em> is a rogue&#39;s art that keepers share — the same net, thrown by either. <em>Quickening Balm</em> is shared the other way: the adepts mix it, and in a keeper&#39;s hands it tends only the beasts.</p><h2 id="arts-worked-on-the-map" tabindex="-1">Arts worked on the map <a class="header-anchor" href="#arts-worked-on-the-map" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Arts worked on the map&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Studied like any other, but used between fights from the <strong>Skills</strong> sheet — once a day each.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Who</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>🧷 Mend the Column</td><td>Alchemist</td><td>Dresses the whole party&#39;s wounds at once: a quarter of every soldier&#39;s health</td></tr><tr><td>🪨 Immovable Object</td><td>Alchemist</td><td>Calls up a boulder. On the map it shuts a tile for good — nothing routes through it again</td></tr><tr><td>💥 Unstoppable Force</td><td>Alchemist</td><td>The same boulder, or on the field a shove that puts a foe two tiles back. If a drop is behind them, they take the fall</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="more-arts-of-the-field" tabindex="-1">More arts of the field <a class="header-anchor" href="#more-arts-of-the-field" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;More arts of the field&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Who</th><th>Used?</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>🔁 Lookout</td><td>Warrior</td><td>active</td><td>Changes places with an ally within walking distance. It costs the march, not the blow — both of you can still fight</td></tr><tr><td>🫳 Steal</td><td>Rogue</td><td>active</td><td>Lifts a draught or charter off a foe in reach. They do not get it back</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="reading-the-research-screen" tabindex="-1">Reading the research screen <a class="header-anchor" href="#reading-the-research-screen" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Reading the research screen&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Open any city&#39;s <strong>Research</strong> tab. The list is ordered by <strong>what an art asks for</strong>: whatever is on the bench first, then everything that could go on it today, then what is still shut — cheapest gate first — and what you have already mastered at the bottom. Each row says what it wants in its own words: &quot;needs hall 2&quot; for a Town Hall study, &quot;needs a Shadow Guild (level 2)&quot; for a trade-hall one.</p><p>The <strong>pills</strong> across the top cut the list down: <em>All</em>, <em>Open</em> (only what can be started today), or one calling at a time. An art two callings share — the net — shows under both.</p><p>Tap any row and the panel on the right explains it and carries the button. Upgrading any one city to level 3 opens the masterworks for the whole guild.</p>',54)])])}const b=e(h,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,b as default};
